  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Calm Ledger",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Calm Ledger\"**\n\nCalm Ledger makes financial education feel like a usable personal space. Green-tinted paper, forest ink, aligned monetary figures, and quiet surface steps give calculators the readability of a well-kept notebook. Direct titles introduce the task; short explanations and familiar controls keep the next action clear.\n\nThe system is mobile first. Its signature is a protected scrolling area above a reachable action dock: a primary action must never cover the content it acts on. Desktop adds a persistent sidebar and room for side-by-side tools while keeping the same hierarchy. Light and dark themes preserve these roles rather than introducing a separate visual identity.\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n\n- Paper-like tonal surfaces with restrained forest accents.\n- Direct headings, readable controls, and aligned monetary figures.\n- Protected content above thumb actions and persistent navigation.\n- Quiet state changes that respect device and user motion preferences.\n\nImplementation authority: `src/styles/theme.css` owns palette, type sizes, spacing, and radii. `src/styles/app.css`, `src/sections/Navigation.css`, and `src/sections/RepeatSales.css` apply those roles. The YAML above records the shipped values; it does not introduce a second implementation theme.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Paper-like tonal surfaces with restrained forest accents.",
      "Direct headings, readable controls, and aligned monetary figures.",
      "Protected content above thumb actions and persistent navigation.",
      "Quiet state changes that respect device and user motion preferences."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Semantic Pair Rule.",
        "body": "Resolve every foreground and surface through the current theme; never carry a light-mode fill or its foreground into dark mode on its own.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Floor Rule.",
        "body": "Body text and inputs stay at 16px; reserve 14px and 12px for metadata and compact supporting labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Direct Heading Rule.",
        "body": "Begin a screen or section with its useful title; do not prepend decorative eyebrow labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Protected Scrollport Rule.",
        "body": "End the content viewport above every fixed action dock and navigation bar; adding bottom padding alone does not establish this relationship.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Depth Rule.",
        "body": "Use surface tone and borders for structure; reserve the soft dock shadow for a floating primary action.",
        "section": "elevation-depth"
      },
      {
        "name": "Learning paths",
        "body": "Three paths group nine tools. Order is instructional; visits are not completion. Keep lesson controls available and use disclosure for detail.",
        "section": "components"
      },
      {
        "name": "Basket and projection",
        "body": "Keep product selection and scenario inputs findable. Use a visible catalog/basket switch and a native period select. Plot before fine-grained controls; no tall sticky result pane.",
        "section": "components"
      }
